COLUMNS
int ID
int FileDataID // a texture of the liquid type, by FileDataID (0 on the rows that stand for a procedural texture): proven from the bytes and by reading the files
int OrderIndex // the row's place among its liquid type's rows, 0 to n-1: proven from the bytes
int Field_02 // -1, or 0 to 2 on the rows whose FileDataID is 0 (which procedural texture each stands for is inferred from the type's own templates): not read
int LiquidTypeID // the liquid type the row belongs to, from the section's relationship map: proven from the bytes

COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's liquid catalogue (wow::LiquidCatalog, docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md 1.4). The
COMMENT layout comes from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: every column the catalogue reads (database.xml,
COMMENT table LiquidTypeXTexture) was checked against the clients' own bytes. A type's rows in OrderIndex order are its
COMMENT LiquidType.Texture templates expanded (a %d template frames 1 to FrameCountTexture, a plain path one row, an empty
COMMENT slot none). Classic Era's table has no rows (and no section). Its hash is the same in Retail 12.1.5, Classic Era
COMMENT 1.15.9, MoP Classic 5.5.4 and Classic Beta 1.60.1. A layout not listed here is not read.

LAYOUT 7BEECC7F
BUILD 12.1.5.70448, 1.15.9.70003, 5.5.4.70449, 1.60.1.70450
COMMENT 3 fields in each of the four clients; IDs in the section's ID list, the liquid type in its relationship map.
